# Test case for probe_eddy_current support on an ARM MCU (renode
# STM32G0B1) - the tap-family commands run end-to-end here (no
# emulator_skip_gcode): the fast host link keeps clocksync clean, which
# the AVR eddy.test's 250 kbaud link cannot (see eddy.fixture.json).
# The gcode is tap-focused: the default-method BED_MESH_CALIBRATE and
# METHOD=scan variants stay covered end-to-end by the AVR eddy.test;
# repeating them here would roughly double the test's wall cost
# (renode tick advances cost ~ms each and the 400 SPS LDC poll wakes
# the firmware ~800x per sim second) without adding coverage.
#
# The log assertions prove the tap sequence actually completed AND
# succeeded - without them a deadline-truncated run would pass
# silently (the emulator path treats deadline-without-crash as
# success and relies on log assertions for completion). The CONTAINS
# lines print in both emulator and fileoutput mode (verified); the
# NOT_CONTAINS lines are the tap-success discriminators: TAP_CALIBRATE
# tolerates a failed final tap with a "Warning! Last tap did not
# succeed." instead of an error, so without them a tap that fires but
# fails pullback analysis would still pass the exit-code check.
CONFIG eddy_arm.cfg
DICTIONARY stm32g0b1.dict
EMULATOR eddy_arm.fixture.json
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "bed will contact at z="
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "estimate contact at z="
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Unable to detect tap"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Last tap did not succeed"

G28
G1 F6000

G1 Z1
G1 X1
G1 Y1

G1 Z2
BED_MESH_CALIBRATE METHOD=rapid_scan

G1 Z5 X0 Y0

PROBE_EDDY_CURRENT_TAP_CALIBRATE

PROBE METHOD=tap

PROBE_EDDY_CURRENT_TAP_CALIBRATE

G1 Z5
PROBE

G1 Z9
